'''Zamboanga Sibugay's 1st congressional district''' is one of the two [[congressional districts of the Philippines]] in the province of [[Zamboanga Sibugay]]. It has been represented in the [[House of Representatives of the Philippines|House of Representatives]] since 2007.<ref name="congleg">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/legislators/?v=province |title=Roster of Philippine legislators |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 19, 2021}}</ref> It was created after the 2006 reapportionment that divided the province into two congressional districts.<ref name="apportion">{{cite web|url=https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/2006/10/26/republic-act-no-9360/ |title=Republic Act No. 9360 |date=26 October 2006 |publisher=[[Official Gazette (Philippines)]] |accessdate=February 19, 2021}}</ref> The district is composed of the eastern municipalities of [[Alicia, Zamboanga Sibugay|Alicia]], [[Buug]], [[Diplahan]], [[Imelda, Zamboanga Sibugay|Imelda]], [[Mabuhay, Zamboanga Sibugay|Mabuhay]], [[Malangas]], [[Olutanga, Zamboanga Sibugay|Olutanga]], [[Payao, Zamboanga Sibugay|Payao]] and [[Talusan, Zamboanga Sibugay|Talusan]]. It is currently represented in the [[20th Congress of the Philippines|20th Congress]] by [[Marlo Bancoro]] of [[Partido Federal ng Pilipinas]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=House Members - 20th Congress |url=https://www.congress.gov.ph/house-members |access-date=2026-07-17 |website=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]]}}</ref>
